nltools - Newline caching and quick seeking suite

                                   RATIONALE

nltools is a simple suite.  It contains the following tools.

        nlcache     Builds a newline lookup table in nlcache file format

        nlseek      Reads a nlcache file and locates the position in the actual
                    file, with prefix matching capability, returning the
                    contents of said line

                                  APPLICATIONS

nltools is useful when a text file needs to be queried by line number quickly
without being a debugging headache.  nlcache produces the newline lookup table
and nlseek merely finds the corresponding line, checking a prefix if it was
given one and returning the rest of the line unprocessed.

                                MORE INFORMATION

In the `man` directory, there are groff files to be used with the man macro
class.  Any working copy of the `man` utility should be able to read them,
formatted.  If one does not have said `man` utility, the files are markup texts
anyway, and should be able to be read with any standard text editor.  It is
recommended that this text editor use a monospace font, since these texts are
meant to be read with such formatting, this file included.

                   +----------------------------------------+
                   | nlcache >> man/nlcache.1  nlcache(1)   |
                   | nlseek  >> man/nlseek.1   nlseek(1)    |
                   +----------------------------------------+

